215 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 99 0 R/E(The Computer Society of India \(CSI\), established on 6th March 1965, is the first and largest professional body for computer professionals in India. Since its inception, CSI has grown into a significant national organization, representing the interests of over 100,000 members across the country.)/Pg 13 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

216 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 99 0 R/E(Founded by a group of visionary computer professionals, CSI has played a crucial role in fostering the growth of computer science and information technology in India. Under the leadership of Professor Rangaswamy Narasimhan, the first president of CSI, the society formed strong connections with global technological bodies, such as the International Federation for Information Processing \(IFIP\).)/Pg 13 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

217 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 99 0 R/E(From the very beginning, CSI has served as a platform for professionals to exchange knowledge, collaborate on research, and contribute to the advancement of computing in India. The society has been pivotal in shaping policies, organizing conferences, and offering opportunities for skill enhancement through various training and certification programs.)/Pg 13 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

218 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 99 0 R/E(Over the years, CSI has expanded its reach across various sectors, including education, industry, and government, providing a unified voice for Indian IT professionals. It continues to champion technological innovation, bridging the gap between academia and industry, and promoting the welfare of computer professionals in India.)/Pg 13 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

219 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 99 0 R/E(To foster a community of excellence in computing and information technology by nurturing innovation, collaboration, and professional growth among students.)/Pg 13 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

220 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 99 0 R/E(To promote knowledge sharing and skill development in the field of information technology and emerging domains.)/Pg 13 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

221 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 99 0 R/E(To provide a platform for students to engage in technical, professional, and ethical practices.)/Pg 13 0 R/K[12]>>
