541 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 113 0 R/E(Under the aegis of the CSI Student Chapter, the Department of Information Technology at St. Vincent Pallotti College of Engineering & Technology organized \215Think Tank Talk\216 on 23rd July 2025. Mentored by faculty coordinator  Prof. Jagdish Pimple and student coordinators Mr. Vedant Joshi, Ms. Anushka Pannase, and Ms. Aditi Dhawad \(all 7th Semester IT\), the session brought together 57 students from the 5th semester IT cohort for an engaging exercise in structured tailor problem-solving and ideation. The initiative was knowledge with practical reasoning, encouraging participants to analyze real-world obstacles through an engineering mindset. Stepping away from traditional academic routines, the floor transformed into a vibrant brainstorming hub where students were invited to identify persistent day-to-day dilemmas and pitch feasible, innovative remedies.)/Pg 27 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

542 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 113 0 R/E(The presentations spanned a diverse spectrum of themes\204from campus workflows and mental well-being to digital ethics, environmental sustainability, and technological accessibility. By articulating their viewpoints in front of peers, speakers not only exercised critical thinking but also adopted a proactive, solution-oriented approach toward societal challenges. Beyond ideation, the event cultivated vital soft skills, fostering active listening, articulate public speaking, and constructive peer dialogue. The positive engagement reflected the cohort\220s enthusiasm for collaborative discourse and creative problem framing. In line with the core mission of the CSI Student Chapter, Think Tank Talk reaffirmed the department\220s drive to empower future engineers with the confidence, analytical agility, and communicative clarity needed to shape real-world impact.)/Pg 27 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

