566 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 115 0 R/E(St. Vincent Pallotti College of Engineering and Technology, Department of Information Technology, under the CSI Student Chapter, successfully conducted an SIH Mentorship Webinar on 14th September 2025, from 2:00 PM to 3:00 PM via Google Meet. The webinar aimed to guide students in transforming innovative ideas into practical solutions, enhancing their problem-solving and teamwork abilities, and preparing for the Smart India Hackathon \(SIH\) and other national-level innovation competitions.)/Pg 29 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

567 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 115 0 R/E(The session covered essential aspects of hackathon preparation, including team formation, problem statement analysis, solution development, idea presentation, and strategic planning. Mr. Jatin Vishwakarma shared his experiences, discussed the challenges encountered during hackathons, and offered valuable strategies for achieving success at the national level. An interactive question-and-answer session further enabled participants to resolve their queries and gain practical insights.)/Pg 29 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

568 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 115 0 R/E(A total of 145 students registered for the webinar from various departments, including IT, CSE, AI, Cyber Security, Data Science, Electrical, Civil, CSBS, IoT, and ETC.)/Pg 29 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

569 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 115 0 R/E(The session enhanced students' understanding of hackathon preparation, innovation, teamwork, and time management. It received an average feedback rating of 4.46 out of 5 from 28 responses, with participants appreciating the informative content and clear explanations.)/Pg 29 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

570 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 115 0 R/E(Overall, the webinar encouraged students to develop practical solutions, strengthen their problem-solving skills, and participate confidently in national-level competitions. The positive feedback reinforced the CSI Student Chapter's commitment to promoting technical learning, innovation, and student development.)/Pg 29 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

