<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 118 0 R/E(The Department of Information Technology at St. Vincent Pallotti College of Engineering and Technology, under the CSI Student Chapter, successfully organized a workshop on \215Generative AI for 10X Impact\216 on 9 December 2025 for third-year students. The session was led by Mr. Govind Chandak, Business Head at NSDM India & GrowthAcad, Pune, who introduced students to practical Generative AI tools and demonstrated how they can enhance productivity, creativity, and problem-solving capabilities. Held in the IT Lab, the workshop witnessed enthusiastic participation from 60 CSI student members, who explored real-world applications of Generative AI through hands-on demonstrations and practical examples.)/Pg 32 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

610 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 118 0 R/E(The workshop featured interactive discussions, demonstrations of AI-powered tools, and a question-and-answer session that enabled students to clarify their doubts and explore emerging AI-driven opportunities. Participants gained valuable insights into integrating Generative AI tools into academic activities and future professional roles, developing greater confidence in exploring innovative AI-based solutions. Conducted under the guidance of Faculty Coordinator Prof. Jagdish Pimple, with student coordinators Shreya Ghodmare and Shantanu Mangalkar of the fifth semester, Information Technology, the workshop proved to be an enriching learning experience. Feedback was collected through a Google Form, and the event reinforced the CSI Student Chapter\220s commitment to equipping students with future-ready skills and encouraging the responsible and impactful use of emerging technologies.)/Pg 32 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

