857 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 131 0 R/E(CERTIFICATE DETECTION)/Pg 45 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

858 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 131 0 R/E(Abstract - The increasing prevalence of fake academic and professional certificates poses a major challenge for educational institutions and employers. Traditional verification methods are time-consuming, largely manual, and vulnerable to digital tampering. This study proposes a theoretical framework integrating Artificial Intelligence \(AI\) and blockchain technology to enable secure and reliable certificate verification.)/Pg 45 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

859 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 131 0 R/E(The framework uses machine learning, deep learning, and image forensics to identify document alterations and generate authenticity scores. Blockchain technology ensures data integrity by storing unique cryptographic hashes of certificates on a decentralized ledger. During verification, the certificate's hash is compared with the stored value to detect unauthorized modifications.)/Pg 45 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

860 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 131 0 R/E(By combining AI-based forgery detectionwith blockchain authentication, the proposed framework aims to improve verification accuracy, enhance security, and build trust in academic and professional credential management.)/Pg 45 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

